<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is Klay Thompson Paid the Mid-Level Exception?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Klay Thompson is paid <strong>$5.6m</strong> because he is 36 and two serious injuries took away several seasons, and the mid-level exception is what is left at that point.</p>
<ul>
<li>He won four championships with Golden State between 2015 and 2022.</li>
<li>Golden State gave him <strong>$189.9m</strong> over five years in 2019, weeks after he tore a knee ligament in the Finals.</li>
<li>He missed two full seasons and was paid <strong>$68.1m</strong> across them.</li>
<li>He was paid <strong>$43.22m</strong> in 2023-24 and is on <strong>$5.6m</strong> three years later.</li>
<li>He has made more three-pointers than all but a handful of players in the game’s history.</li>
</ul>
<p>He has earned <strong>$306.83m</strong> and this season pays under 2% of it.</p>

</div><div class="bde-shortcode-506-159 bde-shortcode"><div class="nba-fin" data-nba-fin="why">
